-- title:
--   Ideal membership in A[σ] is Zariski-local on Spec A
-- statement:
--   Let $\sigma$ be a type of variables and $A$ a commutative ring, let $\iota$ be a type and $r : \iota \to A$ a family of elements of $A$ whose range generates the unit ideal, i.e. $\mathrm{span}(\mathrm{range}\,r) = \top$ in $A$. Let $I$ be an ideal of the multivariate polynomial ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \sigma\ A$ and let $f$ be a polynomial in that ring. The assertion is an equivalence: $f \in I$ if and only if for every index $i : \iota$, the image of $f$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \sigma\ A \to \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \sigma\ (\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,(r_i))$ induced by the structure map $A \to A[1/r_i]$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $I$ under that same ring map, that is, in $I \cdot A[1/r_i][\sigma]$. Here $\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,(r_i)$ is the localisation of $A$ inverting the powers of $r_i$, and $\mathrm{Ideal.map}$ denotes the pushforward of an ideal along a ring homomorphism.
--
--   This is the statement that membership in an ideal of a polynomial ring is local on the base: it suffices to test membership after inverting each member of a family of elements generating the unit ideal, the affine form of the principle that a section of a quasi-coherent sheaf vanishes iff it vanishes on a Zariski cover. It is used in the construction of the Hilbert functor, in the criterion characterising when a closed immersion locally of finite presentation factors through a given subscheme in terms of membership of homogeneous elements.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_mem_ideal_iff_forall_map_mem_map_localizationAway.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
